IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bca-gambler`

-- Betting Control Act 1954 (WA), ss 10J, 21-28, 32 -- worked cases from the gambler's seat.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or regulations (none deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_betting-control-act-1954_baseline.py).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake): k080, 1 September 2045, Jake, 39, bets on apps.
-- Which apps and events is the encoder's choice: the TAB app on a race at Ascot, an app licensed in the Northern Territory
-- on an AFL match in Melbourne, an offshore site on an English football match. His daughter Ruby is 12.

§ `fixtures`

`Jake on the TAB app, Ascot race` MEANS `My bet` WITH
    `who I bet with` IS `the TAB run by RWWA`
    `my age in years` IS 39
    `I am in WA when I make it` IS TRUE
    `I make it by telephone or online` IS TRUE
    `it is a fixed odds bet` IS TRUE
    `the event is outside WA` IS FALSE
    `the Commission has approved bookmaking on the event under s 4B` IS FALSE
    `betting on the event is permitted by the law of another State or Territory` IS TRUE
    `the event is a prescribed prohibited event or contingency` IS FALSE
    `I know, or would be expected to know, the operator is not authorised` IS FALSE
    `the bookmaker takes it as the Act allows` IS FALSE
    `it is social gambling or permitted gaming under the Gaming and Wagering Commission Act 1987` IS FALSE

