§ `s 27A -- interstate and offshore bets`

#ASSERT `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet` `Jake on an NT app, Ascot race`

#ASSERT `Is the operator an authorised person` `Jake on an exempted offshore site, English football`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the operator an authorised person` `Jake on an offshore site, knowing, English football`

#ASSERT `Is it a permitted event` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne`
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a permitted event` `Jake on an NT app, a prohibited event interstate`

#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 27A` `Jake on an offshore site, knowing, English football`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I commit an offence under s 27A` `Jake on an offshore site, not knowing, English football`
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 27A` `Jake on an NT app, a prohibited event interstate`

§ `what the Act makes of my bet`

-- k080: Jake, 39, on the betting apps (the first three and the offshore site).
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot race` EQUALS `lawful: the Act allows it`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on an offshore site, knowing, English football` EQUALS `an offence by me`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Ruby on the TAB app` EQUALS `an offence by me`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake with a bookie at Ascot` EQUALS `lawful: the Act allows it`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake with a licensed bookie outside the rules` EQUALS `an offence by me`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake with an SP bookie at the pub` EQUALS `an offence by me`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on a footy tipping pool at work` EQUALS `lawful: the Act allows it`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on a wagering licensee fixed odds bet` EQUALS `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on the TAB app while in Melbourne` EQUALS `outside the Act: I am not in WA`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot race` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet` `Ruby on the TAB app` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet` `Jake with an SP bookie at the pub` EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet` `Jake on an offshore site, knowing, English football` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS 100000

§ `other offences on the gambler`

-- Ruby (12) asks Jake to put a bet on for her: the encoder's illustration.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for` `place a bet or collect winnings for a person apparently under 18 (s 22A)` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for` `as a person under 18, ask someone to place a bet or collect winnings for me (s 22(1)(c), (d), (2)(c), (d))` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for` `take liquor into a place where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(c))` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for` `place a bet for, or help someone bet with a bookmaker who is under a s 25 court order (s 23(2))` EQUALS 20000

#ASSERT `Must my betting money be forfeited` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `May a bookmaker or the TAB take my bet` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May a bookmaker or the TAB take my bet` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `May the wagering licensee give me credit`

§ `s 25 -- the court order`

#ASSERT `Can the Court order that no bookmaker bet with me` TRUE
#ASSERT `For how many years at most can the order last` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act say who may apply for the order`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I commit an offence by betting while under the order`

§ `s 32 -- disputes`

#ASSERT `Within how many days must I appeal` TRUE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I appeal` FALSE EQUALS 7

#ASSERT `How much must the bookmaker pay me now` 500 200 EQUALS 300

